{{was wotd|2009|October|30}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mer-|id=die}}
From {{der|en|la|morbidus||diseased}}, from {{m|la|morbus||sickness}}, itself from the root of {{m|la|morī||to die}} or directly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mer-||to rub, pound, wear away}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɔː.bɪd/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɔɹ.bɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-morbid.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-morbid.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|originally}} Of, or relating to [[disease]]. {{defdate|from 1650s}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Taking an [[interest]] in, or [[fixating]] on, [[unhealthy]] or [[unwholesome]] subjects such as [[death]], [[decay]], [[disease]]. {{defdate|from 1770s}}
# Suggesting the [[horror]] of [[death]]; [[macabre]] or [[ghoulish]].
# [[grisly|Grisly]] or [[gruesome]].

